<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>Mentora Student App — Supuni Dissanayake</title>
<meta name="description" content="A Flutter client built end-to-end against a live production backend — course discovery, AI-matched recommendations, and the full enrollment lifecycle." />
<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,500;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap');

  :root {
    --ink: #14181d;
    --surface: #1b2129;
    --surface-2: #212934;
    --border: #2a323c;
    --text: #e9e6df;
    --text-dim: #9ba3ac;
    --text-faint: #6b7280;
    --amber: #d9a441;
    --amber-soft: #e8c07a;
    --teal: #4fb3a3;
    --teal-soft: #7ecdc0;
    --danger: #d97757;
    --shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
    :root:not([data-theme="dark"]) {
      --ink: #f4f2ed;
      --surface: #ffffff;
      --surface-2: #faf8f3;
      --border: #e3ded0;
      --text: #21252b;
      --text-dim: #5b6472;
      --text-faint: #8a8f97;
      --amber: #a8752a;
      --amber-soft: #8a5f20;
      --teal: #2a8577;
      --teal-soft: #1f6c60;
      --shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
    }
  }

  :root[data-theme="light"] {
    --ink: #f4f2ed;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --surface-2: #faf8f3;
    --border: #e3ded0;
    --text: #21252b;
    --text-dim: #5b6472;
    --text-faint: #8a8f97;
    --amber: #a8752a;
    --amber-soft: #8a5f20;
    --teal: #2a8577;
    --teal-soft: #1f6c60;
    --shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: "IBM Plex Sans", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  ::selection { background: var(--amber); color: #14181d; }

  a { color: var(--teal-soft); }
  a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible, [tabindex]:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--teal);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-family: "Fraunces", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  code, .mono {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
  }

  .page {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 88px 24px 120px;
  }

  /* ---------- Header ---------- */

  .kicker {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal-soft);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .kicker::before {
    content: "";
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--teal-soft);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal-soft) 25%, transparent);
    flex: none;
  }

  h1.title {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.1rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  h1.title em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--amber-soft);
  }

  .dek {
    margin-top: 18px;
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .meta-row {
    margin-top: 36px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .meta-cell {
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 16px 18px;
  }
  .meta-cell .k {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
  .meta-cell .v {
    margin-top: 5px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ---------- Sections ---------- */

  section { margin-top: 76px; }

  .section-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .section-num {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    flex: none;
  }
  h2.section-title {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  p { color: var(--text-dim); margin: 14px 0; max-width: 66ch; }
  p.lead { color: var(--text); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ---------- Stack tags ---------- */

  .tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .tag {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    padding: 6px 11px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-dim);
    background: var(--surface);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .tag.built { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--amber) 45%, var(--border)); color: var(--amber-soft); }
  .tag.consumed { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 45%, var(--border)); color: var(--teal-soft); }

  .legend {
    margin-top: 14px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 20px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; }
  .dot.built { background: var(--amber); }
  .dot.consumed { background: var(--teal); }

  /* ---------- Architecture diagram ---------- */

  .arch {
    margin-top: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 22px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .arch-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 96px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: stretch;
    padding: 12px 0;
  }
  .arch-row + .arch-row { border-top: 1px dashed var(--border); }
  .arch-label {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    padding-top: 10px;
  }
  .arch-boxes {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .arch-box {
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 9px 13px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .arch-box.core {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 50%, var(--border));
    color: var(--teal-soft);
  }
  .arch-flow {
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ---------- Phase timeline ---------- */

  .phase {
    position: relative;
    padding: 4px 0 4px 44px;
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .phase:not(:last-child) {
    padding-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .phase::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 15px;
    top: 30px;
    bottom: -6px;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--border);
  }
  .phase:last-child::before { display: none; }
  .phase-num {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--amber-soft);
  }
  .phase-title {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .phase-desc {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
  }
  .phase.added .phase-num { color: var(--teal-soft); }

  /* ---------- Bug log ---------- */

  .bug {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--danger);
    border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .bug-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--danger);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .bug-title {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .bug-body { margin: 6px 0 0; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.95rem; }

  /* ---------- Skills ---------- */

  .skills {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .skill {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    padding: 9px 14px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  footer {
    margin-top: 100px;
    padding-top: 26px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .back-link {
    position: fixed;
    top: 18px;
    left: 18px;
    z-index: 50;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 9px 16px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--teal-soft); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .page { padding: 56px 18px 90px; }
    .meta-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .arch-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .arch-label { padding-top: 0; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<a class="back-link" href="/#projects">&larr; Portfolio</a>

<div class="page">

  <header>
    <div class="kicker">Portfolio Case Study — Mobile Engineering</div>
    <h1 class="title">Mentora <em>Student App</em></h1>
    <p class="dek">
      A Flutter client for Mentora, a Sri Lankan tutoring marketplace — course discovery, an
      AI-matched recommendations engine, and the full enrollment lifecycle, built end-to-end
      against a live, pre-existing production backend rather than a spec or a mock.
    </p>

    <div class="meta-row">
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <div class="k">Role</div>
        <div class="v">Sole app-side build</div>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <div class="k">Platform</div>
        <div class="v">Flutter — Android · iOS · Web</div>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-cell">
        <div class="k">Backend</div>
        <div class="v">Node/Express + PostgreSQL (pre-existing, consumed)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-num">01</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Overview</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">
      The Mentora backend already existed — a working tutoring-marketplace API with courses,
      tutors, enrollments, and an AI recommendation endpoint — but had no client. The brief was
      to build the entire <strong>student-facing</strong> app from an empty <code>flutter
      create</code> scaffold: authentication, course browsing, profile management, the
      booking/enrollment flow, and an AI-powered "For You" matching tab, all wired to that real
      backend from day one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tutor-side, admin, communities/feed, and real-time (Socket.io) features were explicitly
      out of scope — this is the student's app, not the whole platform.
    </p>

    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag built">Flutter</span>
      <span class="tag built">Dart</span>
      <span class="tag built">Provider</span>
      <span class="tag built">flutter_secure_storage</span>
      <span class="tag built">image_picker</span>
      <span class="tag consumed">Node.js / Express</span>
      <span class="tag consumed">PostgreSQL</span>
      <span class="tag consumed">Google Gemini</span>
      <span class="tag consumed">REST / JSON</span>
    </div>
    <div class="legend">
      <span><i class="dot built"></i>built in this app</span>
      <span><i class="dot consumed"></i>existing service, integrated</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-num">02</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Architecture</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Provider-based and feature-sliced: every domain — auth, courses, profile, enrollments,
      recommendations — follows the same <code>model → service → provider → screen</code>
      pipeline, so a new feature is additive rather than a rewrite.
    </p>

    <div class="arch">
      <div class="arch-row">
        <div class="arch-label">Screens</div>
        <div class="arch-boxes">
          <span class="arch-box">Auth</span>
          <span class="arch-box">Courses</span>
          <span class="arch-box">For You</span>
          <span class="arch-box">Enrollments</span>
          <span class="arch-box">Profile</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-flow">↕ watch / read</div>
      <div class="arch-row">
        <div class="arch-label">Providers</div>
        <div class="arch-boxes">
          <span class="arch-box">ChangeNotifier state per feature — loading / data / error</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-flow">↕ calls</div>
      <div class="arch-row">
        <div class="arch-label">Services</div>
        <div class="arch-boxes">
          <span class="arch-box">Thin per-feature HTTP wrappers</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-flow">↕ every request</div>
      <div class="arch-row">
        <div class="arch-label">Core</div>
        <div class="arch-boxes">
          <span class="arch-box core">ApiClient — auth header, typed errors, 401 handling</span>
          <span class="arch-box core">TokenStorage — secure, in-memory cached</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:22px">
      The one piece every feature shares is <strong>ApiClient</strong>: it attaches the JWT to
      every request, decodes responses into a typed <code>ApiException</code> on failure, and —
      since the backend has no refresh-token flow — clears the session and forces a re-login the
      moment an existing token is rejected with a 401. A login attempt with a <em>bad
      password</em> also returns a 4xx, but deliberately <em>doesn't</em> trigger that path,
      since no session existed yet to invalidate. Getting that distinction right was the
      difference between "log back in" and an app that silently boots you out while you're still
      typing your password wrong.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-num">03</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">How it was built</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Six incremental phases, each shipped and verified against the live backend before the
      next began — plus two later additions once the core loop was stable.
    </p>

    <div style="margin-top:28px">
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="phase-num">0</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Scaffolding</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">Base-URL strategy (per-platform default, <code>--dart-define</code> override for emulators/devices), the token store, and the API client — before any feature touched them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="phase-num">1</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Authentication</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">Three-step registration (email → OTP → details) matching the backend's verification window exactly, login, forgot/reset password, and session persistence across restarts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="phase-num">2</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Course browsing</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">Public search, filters, pagination, and detail + reviews — reachable with no account, which meant reworking the app's root navigation so browsing wasn't gated behind login.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="phase-num">3</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Student profile</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">Live stats dashboard, photo upload via multipart form data, account deletion.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="phase-num">4</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Enrollments</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">Book, edit, and cancel a class; a status-tabbed list matching the backend's actual enum — new bookings land in <code>requested</code>, not the more intuitive <code>pending</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase">
        <div class="phase-num">5</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Polish &amp; docs</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">Full lint pass, architecture documentation, dead-code removal.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase added">
        <div class="phase-num">+</div>
        <div class="phase-title">AI recommendations</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">A "For You" tab: a preference form (subjects, level, mode, schedule, budget, goal) posted to the backend's Gemini-backed matching endpoint, returning a ranked, per-course match score with a generated explanation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="phase added">
        <div class="phase-num">+</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Visual design pass</div>
        <p class="phase-desc">A custom theme system (palette, type scale, component themes) applied globally, a welcome screen, and a responsive-width fix so the app renders correctly on both a phone and a desktop browser window.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-num">04</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Testing against the real thing</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">
      There was no backend test suite or mock server to build against — so instead of mocking
      responses, almost the entire test suite calls the <strong>live backend</strong> directly:
      real login, real course data, a real create → edit → cancel enrollment round-trip, cleaned
      up after itself either way. That choice is what surfaced the bugs below — they were
      invisible to anything that assumed the API matched its own documentation.
    </p>

    <div class="bug">
      <div class="bug-head"><span>found via live test</span><span>reviews endpoint</span></div>
      <div class="bug-title">A shell tool was lying about the response shape</div>
      <p class="bug-body">
        PowerShell's <code>Invoke-RestMethod | ConvertTo-Json</code> renders a raw JSON array as
        a convincing-looking <code>&#123;"value": [...], "Count": n&#125;</code> object — a display quirk,
        not a real envelope. Trusting it would have shipped a model expecting a wrapper that
        never existed. Re-checking through the actual Dart HTTP client showed
        <code>GET /courses/:id/reviews</code> returns a plain array.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bug">
      <div class="bug-head"><span>found via live test</span><span>enrollment update</span></div>
      <div class="bug-title">PUT silently required the full record, not a patch</div>
      <p class="bug-body">
        Sending only the changed field to <code>PUT /enrollments/:id</code> returned a plain
        400 with no hint why. The endpoint expects the same full field set as
        <code>POST</code> — undocumented, only visible by trying it against the real server.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bug">
      <div class="bug-head"><span>found via live data</span><span>course schedules</span></div>
      <div class="bug-title">Seed data broke the booking form's day/time picker</div>
      <p class="bug-body">
        A meaningful share of courses store <code>schedule</code> as a plain string or
        <code>null</code> instead of the documented <code>&#123;"day": ["times"]&#125;</code> shape — so
        the dropdown had nothing to populate, while the form still demanded a selection. Fixed
        by falling back to free-text day/time entry whenever a course has no structured
        schedule to offer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bug">
      <div class="bug-head"><span>found via manual QA</span><span>images</span></div>
      <div class="bug-title">Broken image URLs decoded as HTML, not pixels</div>
      <p class="bug-body">
        A few course images pointed at dead links that returned an HTML error page with a 200
        status. Flutter's image codec doesn't know that isn't a picture — it just throws. Added
        a themed fallback icon everywhere a network image is used, instead of a raw error
        widget on screen.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="section-num">05</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Skills demonstrated</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="skills">
      <span class="skill">State-management architecture</span>
      <span class="skill">REST API integration</span>
      <span class="skill">Defensive JSON modeling</span>
      <span class="skill">Live integration testing</span>
      <span class="skill">Auth &amp; session handling</span>
      <span class="skill">Responsive Flutter layout</span>
      <span class="skill">Design-system theming</span>
      <span class="skill">Debugging via primary-source verification</span>
      <span class="skill">Working from an imperfect, live backend</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <span>Mentora Student App — engineering case study</span>
    <span>Flutter · Provider · REST</span>
  </footer>

</div>

</body>
</html>
